.DS_Store
.build/

# Lab configuration: addresses, credentials and toolchain paths that
# describe one desk. Start from .env.lab.example; see docs/lab-setup.md.
.env.lab

# Scratch docs: session notes, investigation logs, working plans. docs/
# is published and deliberate; docs/local/ is neither, and keeping them
# in one directory is how the published half stops being deliberate.
# Its README is the exception, because the rule has to be readable.
docs/local/*
!docs/local/README.md

# Agent worktrees, at any depth. A checkout under here is a working copy
# of some branch, not repository content — and one that is tracked goes
# stale silently: five of them reached the index inside the vendored
# Mirror subproject and each answered `Platinum.contentTop` with 22 where
# the live tree says 20, so a grep for that constant found six answers and
# five were wrong. No gate reads a vendored worktree, so nothing catches
# the drift; the cure is to not track them at all.
.claude/worktrees/

build-*/
xcuserdata/
*.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/
*.xcworkspace/


# scripts/q800-68k's session directory: a cloned 1 GB disk image, a build
# tree and screendumps. Disposable by construction, and the disk alone
# would dwarf the repository.
.q800/

# Emulator session scratch: a cloned disk image, the QMP socket, the pid and
# port files a spin-up writes. Same reasoning as .q800 — the clone alone is
# hundreds of megabytes. mirror/ ignores its own run/ separately, because a
# vendored project keeps its own rules.
run/

# Python bytecode from the asset generators in assets/.
__pycache__/
.docs-venv/

# The extracted Platinum asset pack: Apple's own icons, cursors, patterns
# and NFNT strikes, pulled off a local OS 9 image. It is a DEPENDENCY of
# proper rendering, not repository content — 1,154 files and 5 MB of
# somebody else's bitmaps, which reached git as a side effect of wiring
# the pack up rather than as a decision.
#
# It is regenerable, which is what makes this workable: run
# tools/extract-assets-offline against your own image and it lands right
# here. MirrorKitUI's `AssetPack` resolves it at run time and says so
# loudly when it cannot, so an absent pack degrades honestly instead of
# drawing generic art as though it were the guest's own.
# docs/asset-pack.md is the whole story.
mirror/host/MirrorKit/Sources/MirrorKitUI/Resources/

# xcodebuild default output when the app is built from the command line
# rather than Xcode, which uses DerivedData.
now-host/build/

# iconutil build intermediate; appicon.py regenerates it each run.
assets/icons/macos/NewOldWorld.iconset/

# Module cache xcodebuild drops beside the project on command-line builds.
now-host/NewOldWorld.xcodeproj/-Xcc/
tools/gwprobe-out/
